in St. Tammany Parish","/arc-plc/louisiana/st-tammany-parish"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 39 of them. In 2025 the middle sat at 52% for September to October and 53% for October to November. The middle swung the other way in 2026, with May to June at 206%. Grid 12162 had its driest year in 1962 at 59%.</p>"}
